The full Apache 2.0 text is at `libkofemu/bddisasm/LICENSE`, which is the copy
this repository already ships.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Signature sources - bases/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The detection signatures under `bases/` are data rather than program code, and
they carry their own terms: see `bases/LICENSE`. They are kept separate on
purpose. A signature can contain a string lifted from a sample, its value has a
different lifetime from the engine's, and a project may want to place
conditions on redistributing detection data that it would not place on the
scanner that reads it. Deciding both in one file would make that impossible to
change later without reopening every release already made.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`tests/fixtures/` and any sample corpus referenced by the test scripts are
inputs, not part of the Software. Where a fixture is generated it is covered by
the MIT terms above; where one is a third-party artefact it is not redistributed
here, and the scripts that want it say where to get it.
